2026-09-27T01:50:52Z table activity_phenotype.csv rows='All four conclusions rewritten and a grounding pmid added to each of the three measured bins: Non-secretor 7876235, Weak secretor 8981090, Secretor 30345375. Bounds, labels, direction and every other cell unchanged.' (source literature (PubMed/Europe PMC, read in this pass); Curation to 1.1.0: every factual claim in a conclusion now rests on a paper found by literature search in this pass and read. Changes of substance: the norovirus protection is hedged to strong-rather-than-absolute after Carlsson 2009 (19440360); the non-secretor frequency now names the two studies it comes from (20% of Swedish donors, 25% of a British cohort) instead of a bare 1 in 5; the vague 'may be more prone to certain other infections' is replaced by the measured mumps figures from ALSPAC (68% against 48%) and the type 1 diabetes odds ratio from Smyth 2011; the 4-in-5 secretor figure is qualified to European ancestry; the weak bin now states that it covers one partly-working copy beside a non-working one as well as two partly-working ones. No allele activity value was changed - the Vmax measurement in 8981090 (230 against 1030) agrees with the authored 0.25.) by=Anton Kulaga (with Claude) human_reviewed=false
2026-09-27T01:50:52Z table studies.csv file='New table: 11 rows over 10 PMIDs (7876235, 8645240, 8981090, 11606829, 15809881, 16306606, 19440360, 22025780, 30345375, 41132048 twice - once per rsid), each with population and study design transcribed from the paper and one provenance_quote extracted verbatim from the retrieved text.' (source literature (PubMed/Europe PMC, read in this pass); The module stated thresholds and activity values with no grounding evidence at all, which validate_module reported on two of three bins. Every PMID was taken from a literature_search result in this session and its title read back. Each quote was located by hand in the fetch_fulltext output for that PMID and extracted with a regex rather than retyped; curator names the agent that located it. doi is left empty so the enricher's DOI cross-check has something independent to compare.) by=Anton Kulaga (with Claude) human_reviewed=false
2026-09-27T01:50:52Z table licensing.csv file="New table: 13 rows - pubmed and europepmc at layer literature, the module's own MIT row at layer annotation, and one annotation row per cited article carrying that article's own terms." (source lookup_open_access (Unpaywall/Europe PMC) plus each article's own copyright statement; Terms are per article, not per source. Five of the ten cited articles are closed or free-to-read with no licence recorded, so their share_alike, commercial_use and redistribution are left blank - unknown, never false - which correctly drops the module's own commercial-use and redistribution answers to unknown on the published card. Smyth 2011 is CC-BY-NC-ND, so only the single unmodified quoted sentence is carried.) by=Anton Kulaga (with Claude) human_reviewed=false
